sn1.35:2.1 starts: “If one shows oneself in one way
sn1.35:2.2 starts: While actually being otherwise,
sn1.35:2.3 starts: What one enjoys is obtained by theft
sn1.35:2.4 starts: Like the gains of a cheating gambler.”
sn1.39:2.1 starts: “I worship the Buddha, the best of beings,
sn1.39:2.2 starts: Dwelling in the woods at Vesali.
sn1.39:2.3 starts: Kokanada am I,
sn1.39:2.4 starts: Kokanada, Pajjunna’s daughter.
sn1.40:2.1 starts: “Here came Kokanada, Pajjunna’s daughter,
sn1.40:2.2 starts: Beautiful as the gleam of lightning.
sn1.40:2.3 starts: Venerating the Buddha and the Dhamma,
sn1.40:2.4 starts: She spoke these verses full of meaning.
sn1.42:3.1 starts: “The one who gives a residence
sn1.42:3.2 starts: Is the giver of all.
sn1.42:3.3 starts: But the one who teaches the Dhamma
sn1.42:3.4 starts: Is the giver of the Deathless.”
sn1.43:1.1 starts: “They always take delight in food,
sn1.43:1.2 starts: Both devas and human beings.
sn1.43:1.3 starts: So what sort of spirit could it be
sn1.43:1.4 starts: That does not take delight in food?”
sn1.47:1.1 starts: “For whom does merit always increase,
sn1.47:1.2 starts: Both by day and by night?
sn1.47:1.3 starts: Who are the people going to heaven,
sn1.47:1.4 starts: Established in Dhamma, endowed with virtue?”
sn1.47:3.1 starts: “For them merit always increases,
sn1.47:3.2 starts: Both by day and by night;
sn1.47:3.3 starts: Those are the people going to heaven,
sn1.47:3.4 starts: Established in Dhamma, endowed with virtue.”
